From 3d4d7eeb4b02a87ef3345611add28768edf0d9e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:11:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/14] connectd: drop peers that name no networks on a chain
 that shares its genesis

A peer whose init names a network we do not share is dropped already.
A peer that names none is kept, which is right on Bitcoin, where such a
peer can only be a Bitcoin node, and wrong here: LND never sent the
networks field, so a silent peer is almost certainly a Bitcoin LND node
that shares our genesis, and nothing before open_channel tells it
apart. Its gossip queries and ours would cross until then.

On a chain whose chain_hash is not its genesis, a peer that names no
networks is now dropped with a warning that says so. On Bitcoin nothing
changes. --allow-peers-without-networks keeps such peers, for testing
against an implementation that does not send the field.
